('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'multiple_choice', 4, '{"question": "___ finish the report yet?", "audio_text": null, "options": ["Didja", "Whatcha", "Lemme"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'multiple_choice', 5, '{"question": "___ know if you need any help.", "audio_text": null, "options": ["Lemme", "Gimme", "Coulda"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'matching', 6, '{"pairs": [{"left": "didja", "right": "forma reduzida de \"did you\""}, {"left": "doncha", "right": "forma reduzida de \"don''t you\""}, {"left": "whatcha", "right": "forma reduzida de \"what are you\""}, {"left": "gimme", "right": "forma reduzida de \"give me\""}, {"left": "lemme", "right": "forma reduzida de \"let me\""}, {"left": "coulda", "right": "forma reduzida de \"could have\""}]}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'fill_blank', 7, '{"sentence": "___ doing this weekend?", "options": ["Whatcha", "Didja", "Doncha"], "correct": "Whatcha", "translation": "O que você vai fazer neste fim de semana?"}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'fill_blank', 8, '{"sentence": "We ___ finished earlier if we had started on time.", "options": ["coulda", "gimme", "lemme"], "correct": "coulda", "translation": "A gente poderia ter terminado mais cedo se tivesse começado na hora."}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'word_order', 9, '{"words": ["Doncha", "think", "we", "should", "call", "first"], "correct_sentence": "Doncha think we should call first", "translation": "Você não acha que a gente deveria ligar antes?"}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'word_order', 10, '{"words": ["Gimme", "a", "minute", "to", "check", "the", "file"], "correct_sentence": "Gimme a minute to check the file", "translation": "Me dá um minuto pra checar o arquivo"}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'reading', 11, '{"passage": "Beyond modal reductions, native speakers also blend pronouns and auxiliaries into casual contractions. ''Did you'' becomes ''didja'', ''don''t you'' becomes ''doncha'', and ''what are you'' becomes ''whatcha''. ''Give me'' and ''let me'' become ''gimme'' and ''lemme'', and ''could have'' becomes ''coulda''. Recognizing these forms helps learners understand fast, informal speech.", "translation": "Além das reduções de modais, falantes nativos também misturam pronomes e auxiliares em contrações informais. ''Did you'' vira ''didja'', ''don''t you'' vira ''doncha'', e ''what are you'' vira ''whatcha''. ''Give me'' e ''let me'' viram ''gimme'' e ''lemme'', e ''could have'' vira ''coulda''. Reconhecer essas formas ajuda os alunos a entender a fala rápida e informal.", "question": "Why does the text say it is useful to recognize these forms?", "options": ["It helps understand fast, informal speech", "It is required in formal writing", "It replaces standard grammar rules"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'listening', 12, '{"audio_text": "Didja finish the report yet? Whatcha doing this weekend? Lemme know if you need any help.", "question": "What does the speaker offer, according to the audio?", "options": ["To let you know if you need help", "To finish the report", "To do something this weekend"], "correct_index": 0}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'dictation', 13, '{"audio_text": "Gimme a minute to check the file.", "expected": "Gimme a minute to check the file."}'),
('20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000383', 'typing', 14, '{"prompt_pt": "Traduza usando contrações informais: ''Você já terminou? Me avisa se precisar de ajuda.''", "expected": "Didja finish yet? Lemme know if you need any help.", "ai_review": true}'),

